  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The white gear and the black gear closest to the round section of the lens unit are the ones most responsible for the lens's movement. Using tweezers, you can adjust and replace these gears as needed. The white gear should be flush with the rest of the unit while the black gear should occupy the entirety of its cavity.</has_title>
