<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_113282">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_ph00_phillips_screwdriver"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/FlPZZPnhGXmvy1FX.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The motherboard is protected by a silver plate. Remove the two 4.4 mm Phillips #PH00 screws holding the silver cover using the PH00 screwdriver. With the screws removed, lift the cover off of the motherboard.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">15</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/FlPZZPnhGXmvy1FX.standard">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Image"/>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_113290">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_ph00_phillips_screwdriver"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_opening_tool"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/tHWNjNtBKhY3r2SI.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/jDwirXhr3qsS1iho.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Use a plastic opening tool to lift the small black hinge holding the gold ribbon in place at the top of the motherboard. Once the black hinge is lifted, gently slide the ribbon out of the socket. Once the wire is removed, unscrew the three 4.3 mm Phillips #PH00 screws holding the motherboard down using the PH00 screwdriver.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">16</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/tHWNjNtBKhY3r2SI.standard">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Image"/>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/jDwirXhr3qsS1iho.standard">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Image"/>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_113308">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_precision_tweezers"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_opening_tool"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/rSJGg3hHCTYBkass.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/jSibkWjNHerJMy6o.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">With the screws removed, the wires are now able to come off. The wires are connected in two different ways. The RED arrows indicate a small hinge locking the wire in. To remove the wire, follow the same steps taken to remove the wire in the prior steps. The ORANGE markers indicate that you need to lift the wire up and off of the motherboard. Using the opening tool, follow the same steps used to remove the swivel screen wire. For the hinged wires it is recommended that you use tweezers to carefully remove the wire as shown by the RED arrow on the second image. You must carefully remove them by pulling them straight out of the socket they're seated in. It is crucial that you move slowly and carefully! If one of the wires gets damaged, the camera might not work properly after reassembly.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">17</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/rSJGg3hHCTYBkass.standard">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Image"/>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/jSibkWjNHerJMy6o.standard">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Image"/>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_113315">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_tool rdf:resource="#Tool_opening_tool"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/EXMHEquYsTOQVrBU.standard"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/FVKQQ5efIEW3RJgp.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">With the motherboard lifted, remove the indicated wire by using a plastic opening tool. With the first bottom wire removed, the motherboard can be lifted higher, showing two more hidden wires. Remove the wire indicated by the RED arrow by undoing a hinge and sliding the wire out. Remove the wire indicated by the ORANGE arrow by gently pulling it straight out of the socket it is seated in.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">18</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/EXMHEquYsTOQVrBU.standard">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Image"/>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/FVKQQ5efIEW3RJgp.standard">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Image"/>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Step_113318">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Step"/>
  <has_image rdf:resource="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/NWXIy3iMqy6jqSbI.standard"/>
  <has_title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">With every wire properly removed, the motherboard can now be lifted out of the camera.</has_title>
  <has_order rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">19</has_order>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#https://d3nevzfk7ii3be.cloudfront.net/igi/NWXIy3iMqy6jqSbI.standard">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Image"/>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

